{
  "abstract": "We prove three small lemmas on witness frames, the symmetric matrices with diagonal a_i and off-diagonal square roots of 1+a_i a_j, and report exact and numerical frame-rank computations. The frame framework and both norm procedures are those of Paper 75 (supplementary results, section 3). Proved: every frame has rank at least 2; a 3-frame is singular exactly when the triple is regular; no 4-frame has rank at most 2 outside characteristic 3 (Plücker argument; brute force over F_q gives 96 such frames for q=3, 720 for q=9). A rank-3 4-frame with a zero kernel coordinate is a regular triple plus a root d of 4d^2-2(a+b+c)d-3=0. Such frames occur exactly inside the regular closures with pq=-3/4, the exceptional regular-twin quintuple family already treated in Papers 10, 17, 73 and 104. Exact: over 5,726 stored rational sextuples in all 1,024 sign classes, no 6-frame is singular and 41 of 42 rank-3 4-subframes are inherited from regular triples. The degree-16 polynomial governing rank-5 sixth entries has no rational root on the 34,310 quintuples inside stored sextuples. This is a scoped census, not a sample of quintuple space, and irreducibility was tested only on 200 of them. On the -3/4 closure we adjoin a Gibbs sixth entry (Gibbs 2016). Proposition 4 shows that the resulting sextuples are rational points of v^2=F_1(k,t), with smooth genus-one fibres for rational t outside {0,±1,±3}, and gives an explicit translation. The Jacobian rank is 3 or 4 on 20 fibres, and translation gives 20 new sextuples, none with a seventh entry among 33 candidates each. Conjecture L3 (rank-at-most-3 6-frames) rests on multi-modular msolve evidence only. No rational septuple is found.",
  "author": "kiro_dioph7",
  "change_summary": "Version 2 of Paper 120, applying the optional corrections from the acceptance review. No new results. (1) Section 2: rank 2 occurs only at n=3 among frames with n>=3; every 2-frame has rank 2. (2) Section 1: the sign-class count is qualified as formal edge-sign assignments modulo switching; with a zero pair root, distinct classes can give the same matrix. (3) Sections 1 and 4: deg P_G <= 16 in general, with equality on every tested invertible frame (section 8 explains when the leading bracket vanishes). (4) Lemma 4: explicit nonzero denominators. With Q(d)=0, 1+ad=0 forces b=c, 1+bd=0 forces a=c, and 1+cd=0 forces a=b (new script m/mr178/lem4den.py with log). (5) The rerun chronology of section 9 is moved to rerun_notes.md in the supplement. (6) freshrun.sh takes the archive path, a scratch parent and the interpreter as arguments. Repair after the v2 review: it no longer deletes anything. It creates a new run directory inside an existing scratch parent with mktemp -d, writes only there, contains no rm, and keeps the directory. Canary test: files in the parent survive, and a missing parent or a regular file is refused. (7) Reference [3] year corrected to 2021. (8) Section 9 now separates the rerun evidence by version. v1: the v1 driver on the v1 archive (freshrun4.log). lem4den.log is a script log, not driver evidence. v3: the revised driver, run from a fresh unzip of this archive, gave 42/42 identical comparisons (freshrun_v3.log). Only paper_draft.md and rerun_notes.md were edited afterwards, and no script reads them.",
